          "date": "2026-10-20 18:06:10.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "subject": "LU-20999 utils: remove lctl add_conn and del_conn commands",
        "message": "LU-20999 utils: remove lctl add_conn and del_conn commands\n\nlctl add_conn and del_conn injected LCFG_ADD_CONN and LCFG_DEL_CONN\nrecords into a device by hand. Nothing in the test suite, lustre-iokit\nor the man pages uses them, and del_conn was actually sending\nLCFG_DEL_MOUNTOPT, so it never worked as documented.\n\nThe kernel handling of LCFG_ADD_CONN stays, since the MGS config logs\nstill emit it for failover nodes and tgt_mount.c synthesizes it for\nLWP devices. LCFG_DEL_CONN, however, has never been written by the\nMGS or any other in-tree producer, so the kernel path behind it is\ndead: drop the class_process_config() case, class_del_conn(),\nobd_del_conn(), the o_del_conn method and client_import_del_conn().\nThe LCFG_DEL_CONN value itself is kept in the UAPI header since it is\npart of the config record format checked by wirecheck.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7dd160fb1869452a847b1c9a4bd364b46a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
